      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a memo requiring a decisive direction to prevent systemic social collapse, Universal Basic Income is the more objectively stronger bet over targeted welfare programs.\n\nWhile targeted approaches are more cost-efficient in the short term, they often fail to address broad economic shifts and can inadvertently destabilize the population they aim to help through complex eligibility rules.\n\nThe absolute certainty of a guaranteed income floor that UBI offers is far more critical for long-term stability than the partial relief provided by a more efficient but more volatile system.",
